Subject: [PATCH 21/30] =?UTF-8?q?portal:=20Time=20&=20Clock=20settings=20?=
 =?UTF-8?q?=E2=80=94=20sync=20clock=20to=20browser=20+=20NTP=20servers?=
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Add a Time & Clock card to the Settings page for a box with no RTC:

- Sync to browser: POST /settings/time/browser sets the system clock from
  the admin's browser time (date -s @<epoch>), guarded by a 2020-2100
  plausibility check. rnsd tolerates the forward clock step without a
  restart, so setting the clock this way needs no service bounce.
- NTP servers: a minimal editor (store.read/write_ntp_servers) that edits
  only the 'server' lines in /etc/ntp.conf, preserving restrict/comment
  lines and dropping invalid entries; POST /settings/ntp saves and
  /settings/ntp/restart bounces ntpd (S49ntp) to apply.
- The card shows current system time with a synced / not-synced badge and
  a live browser clock.

All three routes are login-gated; the epoch is int-validated (incl.
OverflowError for 'inf') before use, and NTP server names are character-
validated before they reach the config file.
---
